    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e$1.57 a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e for Peshawari kebabs that most people only ever eat at a restaurant.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eCrush whole coriander seeds yourself.\u003c/strong\u003e The whole seed is cheaper than the ground jar and the crunch of the cracked seed is the entire texture of a chapli kebab.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eTomato and onion in the mix stretch the beef.\u003c/strong\u003e That is traditional, not a shortcut, and it is why the meat number stays modest while the patties stay big.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003ePomegranate molasses is one bottle you will keep reaching for.\u003c/strong\u003e It lasts a long time in the fridge and there is no clean substitute for what it does here.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBake, do not fry.\u003c/strong\u003e Frying fourteen servings of patties eats a bottle of oil and an hour of your evening. Sheet pans in a hot oven get you there while you cook the rice."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Crush the whole coriander seeds coarsely, then mix them with the ground cumin, red pepper flakes, chili powder, black pepper, and salt.",
                    "Combine the ground beef with the finely chopped red onion, green onions, minced jalapeno, garlic, ginger, cilantro, eggs, all-purpose flour, pomegranate molasses, and the spice mix.",
                    "Fold in the drained diced tomatoes last and gently, so they stay in pieces instead of turning the mixture to slurry.",
                    "Chill the mixture for thirty minutes, which makes it far easier to shape.",
                    "Form wide, flat, thin patties, brush the sheet pans and the tops with the vegetable oil, and lay them out without touching.",
                    "Bake at 425 degrees, flipping once, until browned and crisp at the edges and cooked through.",
                    "Cook the rice according to the package while the kebabs bake."
                ],
